# {{music}} A [[dissonant]] music [[note]].Used in [[Baroque]] music as a decorative embelishment of a melodic note.  The grace note is played as quickly as possible and takes no time from the melody note.  The symbol for this grace note being a smaller quaver with a line through.

Acciacaturas feature in Grade 5 Theory, by Eric Taylor. They are not always dissonant, and you recognise them by a little note with a line going through it. There can be more than one acciacatura in a row, however this adoption is only used in modern film music; not late Baroque. 

